title: "JWST-Ramp-Slicer"
version: 1.1.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21875189
date-released: 2026-09-08
url: "https://github.com/Corrado777/JWST-Ramp-Slicer"

abstract: >-
  JWST-Ramp-Slicer is a Python tool for calibrating JWST NIRCam ramps into a sequence of group-difference images for improved detection & photometric extraction of moving objects. For a ramp containing N groups, this software produces N-1 calibrated images corresponding to the differences between consecutive group pairs. By shortening the effective exposure time of each image, group differencing reduces trailing losses for moving sources relative to the standard ramp-fit. The resulting images can be used with moving-object-detection workflows such as digital tracking (shift and stack).

